---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-11-15-founders-tour-add-to-calendar.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-11-15',
  title: 'Founders tour confirmation card offers Add to Calendar',
  tags: ['waitlist', 'lead-capture', 'founders', 'tour'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">November 15, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    The Your Tour Is Booked card on
    <a href="/pricing" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing</a> now has Add to
    Google Calendar, Add to Outlook and Add to Apple Calendar buttons.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Why</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The Zoom calendar invite often goes unaccepted, so a booked tour could never reach the
      applicant's calendar and was easy to forget.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">How it works</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The buttons are built in the visitor's browser from the booked start time in the calendar's
      booking message, with the message's end time when it carries one and 90 minutes otherwise.
      The event is titled BreederHQ Founders Tour and points to the Zoom link in the invite from
      admin@breederhq.com. Apple Calendar downloads an .ics file. When no usable start time
      arrives, the buttons are left out. Nothing is sent to BreederHQ.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
